A Look at History
The word astrology designates a field of knowledge more than ten thousand
years old and whose object of studyis the possible influence of the stars on
the earth,on natural phenomena,political events,and,above all,on human
disposition,character and fate.
Let us go back in time to when the foundations of astrology were first
established and place ourselves in the position of early man,who saw him-
self completely at the mercy of the elements:He had to learn the seasons
for gathering and for hunting,and to keep from starving,he had to take
care to have enough food for the times when there was little or no nourish-
ment to be found.As a matter of course,he discovered he had to subject
himself to a cosmic rhythm,the changing seasons,in order to survive.
When the Sun set,it became cold and dark,and the day's activity came to
a compulsory end.Man's existence was dependent on his being active during
the day and taking his rest at night.
Early man,too,was aware of his vital need of the Sun.It is then no wonder
that he began to mark the course of the Sun in order to come to rights with
theimportant phases of life.Observation and experience showed that the Sun
did not rise and set at the same place every day.This is testified,for
example,by the ancientcircle of stones discovered in Scotland.In this
circle,the four cardinal points are marked by blocks of stones.
In another stone circle,located in Northeast Scotland,are contained six
stone blocks indicating not only north,south,east and west,but also south-
southeast and north-northwest,i.e.the winter and summer solstitialpoints.

