ling evidence of this in all parts of the world.
Man's existence has always been threatened and plagued by war,and a cer-
tain role was played here by the planet Mars.Mars in perigee shone most
brightly in a reddish light.Early man knew from experience that a period
of a red-tinted Mars in perigee frequently meant great tribal unrest and
animosities,and the danger of war was imminent.
Outstanding achievements of ancient man were the grouping of the myriad
stars appearing in the firmament into the signs of the zodiac and the exact
measurement of the solar,lunar,and planetary motion within the zodiac.
The oldest representation of the zodiac known is located at the temple at
Dendera in Egypt and dates approximately from the period of the conquest
of Egypt by Alexander the Great (332 B.C.)

